{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Firstborn of his ox.</b> The first king that HaShem chose for Himself from the seed of Joseph — this is Joshua — and he calls him firstborn because he was the first to be crowned of his seed. And he likens the king to an ox because it is king among beasts." "<b>And they are the myriads of Ephraim.</b> The horns — they are the myriads of Ephraim, who were his kinsmen and men of his war." "<b>And they are the thousands of Manasseh.</b> This is Gideon, and he assigned the myriads to Ephraim because Jacob gave him the greatness."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:26.614545090Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}